# Nothing Roland-derived is ever committed. See NOTICE.md.
#
# The first block is the load-bearing one: SCCore.dll is Roland's 24 MB wave ROM, and everything
# generated from it -- extracted tables, differential fixtures, rendered audio -- carries the same
# rights. The generators say so themselves ("Roland-derived output: generate locally, do not
# redistribute"). These patterns are deliberately broad and deliberately first.
SCCore.dll
SCCore*.dll
tables/
fixtures/
*.wav

# Build output
build/
out/
compile_commands.json
.cache/

# vcpkg
vcpkg_installed/

# MSBuild / Visual Studio / WinUI
.vs/
x64/
Debug/
Release/
obj/
bin/
*.user
*.aps
Generated Files/
packages/

# The XAML compiler writes these two into the project directory rather than into "Generated Files"
# with everything else, so they sit among the sources looking exactly like sources. They are not:
# XamlMetaDataProvider.idl is regenerated from the .xaml on every build, and cppwinrt compiles the
# .cpp automatically when CppWinRTOptimized is set. Committing them means the next person's build
# either fights a stale copy or produces a diff nobody wrote.
/src/app/XamlMetaDataProvider.idl
/src/app/XamlMetaDataProvider.cpp

# MSIX packaging and signing. A signing certificate must never be committed.
AppPackages/
BundleArtifacts/
*.pfx
*.cer
*.appx
*.msix
*.msixbundle
